course: dictionary
lesson: 13386
title: Speakers and hearers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hearer is a person who hears or listens to something. When you listen to a story, a speech or a talk, you are its hearer. Hearers can be a whole room of people or just one friend.
explain: Talking has two sides. The speaker is the one who talks, and the hearer is the one who listens. «The hearers sat quietly while the speaker told the story.» Here the speaker tells and the hearers listen.
explain: Good speakers think about their hearers. What do the hearers already know? What do they need to be told? Writers and speakers who think about this are easier to follow.
fact: A hearer is a person who hears or listens to something.
fact: «The hearers clapped loudly at the end of the speech.»
fact: In a conversation, the hearer is the listener, and the speaker is the one talking.
fact: «The speaker and the hearer swapped places when Mia began to answer.»
fact: Hearers of a sermon are the people who listen to a talk given in church.
exercise: «The hearers sat quietly while the speaker told the story.» Who are the hearers? | The person telling the story | The book the story was written in | *The people listening to the story | The room where the story was told
exercise: In a conversation, what is the hearer? | The one who does all the talking | The person who writes the words down | A loud noise in the room | *The listener, who is not the one speaking
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means a person who listens. «The hearer smiled at the speaker.» | sentence | smiled | *hearer | speaker
test: In «the speaker and the hearer», which one is listening? | The book | *The hearer | The speaker | The teacher
test: Which phrase means people who listened to a story? | *Hearers of the story | Storytellers | Story books | Speakers of the room
exam: Why should a good speaker think about the hearer? | To finish the talk as fast as possible | *To choose words that match what the hearer already knows | To talk as loudly as they can | To make the hearer leave the room
